{
  "_comment": "Plural forms per ItemNoun case, per language. English has two categories (one, other). Hebrew has FOUR: one, two, many, other — 'two' is a genuinely distinct form (שתי תמונות), which is the whole reason this app cannot pluralize by appending a letter. CLDR decides which category a number falls into; we only supply the wording. Note the singular forms carry no digit at all ('one photo' / 'תמונה אחת'), which is the natural reading in both languages and is impossible to express with string concatenation.",

